WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.680
Me and my little sister

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.480
going to check my nan
in Birmingham,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.160
that's what we used
to call holidays back then.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.880
What, and you didn't go
to the beach there?

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.880
The beach
in Birmingham, blood?

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.720
-Yeah, ain't there one?
-Are you stupid?

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.320
You're so… Do you know what?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.440
I refuse to believe

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.200
that you're fucking serious
right now.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.400
Where I've been…

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.360
people ain't really
that nice to you.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.680
When they are…

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.480
you kinda always got
your guard up wondering why.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.960
Remember them lavish meals

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.720
you used to cook up in here,
Miss Hill?

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.640
Used to come here
hoping you'd cook.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.600
If I was lucky enough, boy,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.480
come here and got
that ackee and saltfish

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.920
with the dumplings and that.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.480
Yeah.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.880
Don't forget them
times there.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.640
That right there's
my little girl.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.880
When her daddy comes home,

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.640
that little girl…

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.840
used to be standing
in front of her hero.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.960
Not a fucking con
in prison stink.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.200
Here comes the plane.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.640
Go on, here comes the plane.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.760
-How many kids have you got?
-Who said I have kids?

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.680
Look at it.
It's all moving and that.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.320
What are you
gonna do with it?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.400
I'm gonna cook it.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.440
What are you gonna make?

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.760
I'm gonna make lobster.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.080
It's a crab.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.720
Do you believe in unicorns?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.200
No.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.840
Do you believe in aliens?

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:56.920
Yeah.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.960
OK, at least
that's something.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:00.960
These seagulls are bougie.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.280
-They want the fish.
-Can you stop it, please?

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.560
Jas, I always knew
you were scared of birds.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.080
Nothing like that.
I'm not scared of them.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.680
I just don't like them, bro.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.560
It's not funny, fam.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.360
I ain't never seen
you with a bird, as it goes.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.440
And this is my favourite.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.080
The Tiger Who Came to Tea.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.480
What's that about?

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:25.880
A tiger who came to tea.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.480
Makes sense.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.240
"We better open
the door and see."

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.640
"Sophie opened the door

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.320
and there was a big,
furry, stripy tiger.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.840
And the tiger said…"

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.680
You scared me.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.320
If you could have
anything, yeah…

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:03.920
What would it be?

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.560
-Anything?
-Do anything, have anything.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.520
What would it be?

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.720
You know what?
To go watch Arsenal play.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.600
'Cause they're the best
fucking team

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.600
in the whole Premier League.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.160
-To come watch Arsenal?
-Yeah.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.040
A'ight, it's done.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:23.960
No.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:24.960
Yeah.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.160
You lost someone,
didn't you?

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.120
How are you feeling
about that?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:36.640
It's like…

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.440
all this noise
is in my head.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.040
It just don't ever go away.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.560
What, you ain't got no
woman waiting for you?

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.640
Woman waiting for me?

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.680
No, man.
I'm not into all that, man.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:54.400
Not into women, nah?

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.880
Nah, I'm into women,
but it's the relationships.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.480
Yeah, don't worry,
when we get back,

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.400
me and you gonna find
some proper tings.

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:02.600
-Yeah.
-Trust me.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.680
Yeah.

